      "id": "HI-C60-monkey",
      "sequence": 2210,
      "title": "बंदर (bandar) — a monkey",
      "headword": "बंदर",
      "romanization": "bandar",
      "gloss": "a monkey",
      "script": "devanagari",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:0dd5781e7acd6a57",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new run of words: which letter did the piece before this one give you, and where does the tongue go for it?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: बंदर",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "बंदर (bandar) — \"a monkey\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "From Sanskrit वानर (vānara), 'monkey', a word many readers of Sanskrit connect with वन (vana), 'forest' — the one who belongs to the woods. Prakrit wore it down and a nasal crept in at the front, and बंदर (bandar) came out the other end."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Keep one thing straight before you travel. Persian has its own bandar, spelt the same in our letters, and it means a harbour — it is the bandar inside a dozen port names on the Indian Ocean. Two different words that happen to sound alike, not one word with two jobs."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The first of five animals."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "bandar",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *bandar*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "it once more, slowly",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: it once more, slowly]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "bandar, then ghoṛā, and say which of them a house keeps on purpose",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *bandar*, then *ghoṛā*, and say which of them a house keeps on purpose]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What does बंदर (bandar) mean? (\"a monkey\".) Say it once more."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "HI-S140-nuqta",
      "sequence": 2215,
      "title": "◌़ (nuqtā) — the dot you have been reading and nobody named",
      "headword": "़",
      "romanization": "nuqtā",
      "gloss": "the single mark ◌़ — a dot under a consonant, in your reading from the very first words and never once named",
      "script": "devanagari",
      "modality": "pen",
      "derivedModality": "pen",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "writing-type",
        "writing-block",
        "script-block",
        "sight-cue"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:56b0dcbdbacb43d5",
      "notice": {
        "modality": "pen",
        "needs": [
          "a pen and something to write on",
          "your eyes, for letter shapes on the page",
          "your eyes, because the lesson points at something written down"
        ],
        "waitUntilStopped": [
          "Script you'll notice: ◌़",
          "Script: the two that flap",
          "Guided Practice"
        ],
        "text": "Before we start: this one needs your hands, so it is not a driving lesson. You will want a pen and something to write on, your eyes, for letter shapes on the page and your eyes, because the lesson points at something written down. You can listen to everything else now — leave the sections called Script you'll notice: ◌़, Script: the two that flap and Guided Practice until you have stopped, and I will say so again when we reach it."
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two letters you can draw: ड and ढ. Say each one."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Now look at बड़ा and पढ़ना. Something is under the letter in each of them that is not under the bare letter above."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "script",
          "title": "Script you'll notice: ◌़",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "◌़ (nuqtā) — a single dot, sitting below the consonant."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is not a vowel sign. A vowel sign changes the vowel a consonant carries. This one changes the consonant itself into a different sound, and the letter underneath keeps its shape."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Worked through: ड + ◌़ (nuqtā) = ड़."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The order is carrier first, dot second. The reference that defines this mark describes where the dot sits and what it combines with, not the order a hand should move in, so take carrier-first as a convention of this book rather than a rule handed down. Source: The Unicode Consortium, The Unicode Standard, Version 17.0, Core Specification, section 12.1.3 ‘Combining Marks’, U+093C Devanagari Sign Nukta, 2025."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "script",
          "title": "Script: the two that flap",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "table",
              "headers": [
                "letter",
                "with the dot",
                "sound"
              ],
              "columns": 3,
              "rowCount": 2,
              "utterances": [
                "letter: ड. with the dot: ड़. sound: ṛa.",
                "letter: ढ. with the dot: ढ़. sound: ṛha."
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The tongue taps the roof of the mouth once and flicks forward. It is a flap rather than a held sound."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Every one of these was yours long before this page:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "बड़ा — big."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सड़क — road."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "खिड़की — window."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पढ़ना — to read."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सीढ़ी — stair."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Read them again and this time the dot is part of what you are reading. Look at where in each word the dotted letter falls."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "writing",
          "title": "Writing: ◌़ — copy what you see",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Draw the consonant the way you already draw it. Then put one dot below it, under the middle of the letter, clear of the line."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Put your pen on ड़ and follow it. Copy the shape slowly and larger than it is printed."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "This book does not tell you where to start the character or which way to travel. That is a real thing, taught with real variation from school to school, and it is not written down here until it can be written down with a source. Copying what is in front of you needs no such source, and it is how the shape gets into your hand in the meantime."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "LOOK",
              "instruction": "at these two words and find the dot in each",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU LOOK: at these two words and find the dot in each]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सड़क, सीढ़ी."
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "TRACE",
              "instruction": "ड़ three times, saying ṛa as you finish each one",
              "spoken": false,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU TRACE: ड़ three times, saying *ṛa* as you finish each one]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "what the dot changes — the vowel, or the consonant",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: what the dot changes — the vowel, or the consonant]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 5,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Where does ◌़ (nuqtā) sit? (Below the consonant.) What does it change? (The consonant, not the vowel.) Name a word you have read for weeks that carries it."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
