        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: साँप",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "साँप (sā̃p) — \"a snake\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "From Sanskrit सर्प (sarpa), 'snake', built on सृप् (sṛp-), 'to creep'. The animal is named for what it does, and Latin did exactly the same thing: serpēns is 'the creeping one', from the very same ancient root."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "So English serpent and Hindi साँप (sā̃p) are the same word, four thousand years apart, and neither of them borrowed it from the other. The r of सर्प melted into the p, and the nose-vowel you learnt to write is what is left standing where it was."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "sā̃p",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *sā̃p*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "it once more, slowly",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: it once more, slowly]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "sā̃p, then bandar, and say which one you would rather meet",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *sā̃p*, then *bandar*, and say which one you would rather meet]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
