    {
      "id": "HI-C60-peacock",
      "sequence": 2250,
      "title": "मोर (mor) — a peacock",
      "headword": "मोर",
      "romanization": "mor",
      "gloss": "a peacock",
      "script": "devanagari",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:a5f1899197e69776",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Name the 4 words of this chapter so far."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: मोर",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मोर (mor) — \"a peacock\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "From Sanskrit मयूर (mayūra). The y dropped out, the two vowels ran together, and a three-piece word became a one-piece one — the same wearing-down you have watched happen to a dozen words by now."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मयूर itself is still alive in formal Hindi and in names, so the two forms sit side by side: the old one on a wedding card, मोर (mor) in the yard. And the yard is where you meet it — a मोर (mor) walks into a village at dusk the way a pigeon walks into a city square."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Five: बंदर (bandar), साँप (sā̃p), मुर्गी (murgī), भैंस (bhaĩs), मोर (mor). Enough to name what lives around a house you are greeting."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "mor",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
